[h1]Phobos Medical 0.3.0[/h1]
[b]Draft - not published | 2026-10-04[/b]

[h2]Added[/h2]

[list]
[*]The Halewright Vigil-2 Patient Monitor, a two-by-two bedside cart bought whole and installed through INSTALL, APPS. Stand it beside a Ward-3, touching it or one tile away, and its Control Panel shows the patient's blood lost, infection, pain and worst wound, each with its change over the last hour, and every open wound by place with whether it is bleeding, dressed, fractured, splinted or infected.
[*]Alerts. When blood loss, infection or pain rises to its alert level, or a wound starts bleeding, the monitor posts one caution to the crew log and on the navigation screen. It warns again only once the figure has eased and risen again. Alerts can be switched off on its panel.
[*]It only watches. It never treats, heals or moves anyone, and a reading it cannot take says so rather than showing zero. It draws a little power while switched on and more while watching a patient.
[*]Its own Halewright artwork in the Ward-3's style: off-white casing, grey trim, a folded sensor arm, a stowed lead and teal accents, generated by OpenAI's built-in image tool with the Ward-3 as style reference. The owner asked for a larger monitor than the first one-tile plan, so it is a two-by-two cart (Vigil-2).
[*]The care pack gains the monitor's power and an alerts section (bloodLost, infection, pain), each below the game's fatal or knock-out level.
[*]Sold on the same routes as the Ward-3 for 9,500, and for scrip at Warm standing. Repair takes small parts, a mainboard, a screen and aluminium scrap.
[*]F3 console: phobosmedical alerts and bed.
[/list]

[h2]Save compatibility[/h2]

[list]
[*]Automatic. Nothing saved changes; the hour's trend is kept in memory and starts again after a reload.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility and limits[/h2]

[list]
[*]Requires Phobos Framework 0.86.0, which adds the shared touching test.
[*]Offline checks are not gameplay validation; owner gameplay checks are pending.
[/list]
